```java
public static long factorial(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) {
        return 1;
    }
    long result = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        result *= i;
    }
    return result;
}
```

The provided Java code snippet uses recursion to calculate the factorial of a given number, adhering to the defined requirements. The method handles all edge cases, including handling non-positive inputs and successfully completing the computation for any legal inputs.

